WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.317
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.617 --> 00:00:07.574
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:15.170
Unit twenty-seven: Online Life and Privacy. In this unit, you will talk about online safety and imagine different past results.

4
00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:17.324
personal data.

5
00:00:18.024 --> 00:00:22.589
personal data means information about you, like your name, address and phone number.

6
00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:25.759
Never share your personal data with strangers online.

7
00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.612
Your turn. Say: personal data.

8
00:00:31.312 --> 00:00:32.476
personal data.

9
00:00:33.483 --> 00:00:34.090
hacker.

10
00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:38.078
hacker means a person who gets into computers without permission.

11
00:00:38.378 --> 00:00:40.726
A hacker stole thousands of passwords.

12
00:00:41.426 --> 00:00:43.625
Your turn. Say: hacker.

13
00:00:46.325 --> 00:00:47.164
hacker.

14
00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:48.814
phishing.

15
00:00:49.514 --> 00:00:53.325
phishing means fake emails or messages that try to steal your information.

16
00:00:53.625 --> 00:00:56.101
That email from the 'bank' was a phishing attack.

17
00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:59.035
Your turn. Say: phishing.

18
00:01:01.735 --> 00:01:02.481
phishing.

19
00:01:03.483 --> 00:01:04.972
two-step verification.

20
00:01:05.672 --> 00:01:09.506
two-step verification means a login that needs your password and a code.

21
00:01:09.806 --> 00:01:12.305
Turn on two-step verification for your email.

22
00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.866
Your turn. Say: two-step verification.

23
00:01:18.566 --> 00:01:21.204
two-step verification.

24
00:01:22.217 --> 00:01:23.438
profile settings.

25
00:01:24.138 --> 00:01:27.787
profile settings means the options that control who sees your account.

26
00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:31.108
Check your profile settings to keep your photos private.

27
00:01:31.808 --> 00:01:35.435
Your turn. Say: profile settings.

28
00:01:38.135 --> 00:01:39.578
profile settings.

29
00:01:40.583 --> 00:01:41.503
fake account.

30
00:01:42.203 --> 00:01:46.258
fake account means a social media profile pretending to be someone else.

31
00:01:46.558 --> 00:01:48.731
Someone made a fake account using my photo.

32
00:01:49.431 --> 00:01:51.526
Your turn. Say: fake account.

33
00:01:54.226 --> 00:01:55.251
fake account.

34
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.216
report button.

35
00:01:57.916 --> 00:02:01.448
report button means a button to tell a website about harmful content.

36
00:02:01.748 --> 00:02:03.934
Use the report button if you see bullying.

37
00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:06.949
Your turn. Say: report button.

38
00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:10.755
report button.

39
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.041
strong password.

40
00:02:13.741 --> 00:02:18.318
strong password means a long password with letters, numbers and symbols.

41
00:02:18.618 --> 00:02:20.711
A strong password is hard to guess.

42
00:02:21.411 --> 00:02:24.504
Your turn. Say: strong password.

43
00:02:27.204 --> 00:02:28.426
strong password.

44
00:02:29.417 --> 00:02:31.474
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:31.774 --> 00:02:34.737
Someone hacked my social media account yesterday!

46
00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.515
Oh no. Did you have two-step verification turned on?

47
00:02:40.817 --> 00:02:43.945
No. If I had turned it on, they wouldn't have got in.

48
00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.226
Did you click on any strange links?

49
00:02:48.517 --> 00:02:52.493
Yes, a phishing message. If I had checked it, I wouldn't have clicked.

50
00:02:53.783 --> 00:02:58.592
Change to a strong password now, and use the report button for the fake messages.

51
00:02:59.883 --> 00:03:02.312
Grammar focus: Third conditional.

52
00:03:02.612 --> 00:03:06.458
Use the third conditional for imaginary situations in the past.

53
00:03:06.758 --> 00:03:10.696
If plus had plus past participle, then would have plus past participle.

54
00:03:10.996 --> 00:03:15.132
For example: If I had used a strong password, they wouldn't have hacked me.

55
00:03:15.432 --> 00:03:20.973
Use the third conditional to talk about past situations that didn't happen, often to express regret.

56
00:03:21.983 --> 00:03:24.415
Now read and listen. One Click Too Many.

57
00:03:24.715 --> 00:03:28.781
Last year, a university student received a message about a free phone.

58
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:32.512
She clicked the link and typed in her personal data.

59
00:03:33.817 --> 00:03:37.058
Within minutes, a hacker had taken control of her accounts.

60
00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:42.021
If she had used two-step verification, the hacker wouldn't have got in.

61
00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:46.756
Now she teaches her classmates how to recognise phishing messages.

62
00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:50.633
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:50.933 --> 00:03:53.966
Fake messages that try to steal your information are blank.

64
00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:58.372
A, phishing. B, profile settings. C, a report button.

65
00:04:02.383 --> 00:04:03.953
The answer is A: phishing.

66
00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:08.274
If I blank earlier, I wouldn't have missed the bus.

67
00:04:08.574 --> 00:04:11.438
A, left. B, had left. C, would leave.

68
00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.589
The answer is B: had left.

69
00:04:19.083 --> 00:04:21.257
If she had studied, she blank the exam.

70
00:04:21.557 --> 00:04:25.303
A, would pass. B, would have passed. C, passed.

71
00:04:29.317 --> 00:04:31.258
The answer is B: would have passed.

72
00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.224
A long password with letters, numbers and symbols is a blank.

73
00:04:36.524 --> 00:04:40.224
A, strong password. B, fake account. C, hacker.

74
00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:46.437
The answer is A: strong password.

75
00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.971
According to the text, what would have stopped the hacker?

76
00:04:51.271 --> 00:04:55.853
A, a new phone. B, two-step verification. C, a fake account.

77
00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:02.418
The answer is B: two-step verification.

78
00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:08.218
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you do to protect your personal data online?

79
00:05:13.518 --> 00:05:19.592
I use strong passwords, turn on two-step verification and never click links from strangers.

80
00:05:19.892 --> 00:05:21.369
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:22.383 --> 00:05:26.115
Great work today! You learned eight new words and third conditional.

82
00:05:26.415 --> 00:05:31.030
Today's value is online safety. Keep your password secret and be kind online.

83
00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.994
See you in Unit twenty-eight. Goodbye!

84
00:05:34.294 --> 00:05:37.480
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

